From 2ea30634f77eafc749f1e0ceffe6e4bb43c2df08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dominik Raddatz <dominik.raddatz@clyso.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 12:43:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] test: shrink benchmark iterations under any sanitizer

e16e6398b1e cut the bufferlist benchmark rounds to 2 under ASan.
Extend that to all sanitizers with sanitized_bench_rounds(), keyed on
a new CEPH_SANITIZED define (UBSan has no compiler macro of its own),
and use it for csum_bench and the transaction and mem_is_zero()
benchmarks too.  Only pure repetition is cut; every case still runs.

Under TSan (GCC 15.2, Debug), unittest_bufferlist, by far the longest
unit test, drops from about 26 min to 33 s.  unittest_bluestore_types,
one of the longest remaining, drops from about 225 s to 200 s, as its
csum_bench case goes from about 25 s to under 1 s.  unittest_transaction
and unittest_memory drop from about 19 s and 15 s to under 1 s.
Builds without sanitizers are unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Dominik Raddatz <dominik.raddatz@clyso.com>
